From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: NtReadRequestData and NtWriteRequestData

K-LPC leftover (wine-sg 7809). A request may carry data information at
VirtualRangesOffset (a count, then { base, size } entries; the 64-bit
layout, also for 32-bit callers) describing buffers of the sender's. While
the sender waits for its reply, the process that received the request may
read and write those buffers through the port, at most an entry's size;
another message or client id, or a request already replied to, gives
STATUS_REPLY_MESSAGE_MISMATCH. The wineserver keeps the request's data
information from the send (the receiver's copy is not trusted), returns
VirtualRangesOffset to the receiver, and copies with read_process_memory /
write_process_memory (new request port_request_data, protocol 879).
